    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Primal Scream’s XTRMNTR is a ferocious pivot into noise, electronics, and political confrontation, pushing the band’s rock roots into a harsher, more militarized sound. Released in 2000, it became one of their most acclaimed records, built on abrasive guitar squall, distorted drum programming, acid-house pulses, and a confrontational edge that matched the era’s unease. Tracks such as “Kill All Hippies,” “Accelerator,” and “Swastika Eyes” helped define its reputation as a chaotic but tightly controlled assault, with the album widely seen as a high point in the group’s experimental run.\n\nThe 2026 Bunker Trilogy reissue presents XTRMNTR as part of a newly expanded and remastered series alongside Vanishing Point and Evil Heat. Supervised by Bobby Gillespie and Andrew Innes and newly mastered by Matt Colton, this edition restores the original album and adds B-sides, rarities, and previously unreleased material, making it the most comprehensive version of the record to date. Issued by Sony Music, it underscores the album’s lasting importance as a landmark fusion of electronic music and rock aggression.",
